WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.020
The return of the Dilophosaurus and more Ian
Malcom and Maisie are just some of the scenes

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.069
we never got to see in Jurassic World: Fallen
Kingdom.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:12.030
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm revealing the top deleted scenes

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.390
from Jurassic World 2, plus explaining scenes
that were censored for graphic violence.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.810
Spoilers ahead for the movie, so take care
if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.130
Although Fallen Kingdom features more dinosaurs
than ever, there's one fan favourite that

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.260
ended up deleted from the final film.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.279
Director J.A.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:31.100
Bayona revealed a scene with a couple of Dilophosaurus
was cut from the movie.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
The Dilo first appeared in the original Jurassic
Park and, let's face it, who can forget that

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:44.470
scene where Dennis Nedry gets his comeuppance?

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:48.710
It seems like the Dilophosaurus was supposed
to appear in Fallen Kingdom's opening scene

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.719
where the guy in the yellow jacket, who was
operating the mosasaur gate, was startled

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.480
by a rustling in the bushes along with a little
chirp reminiscent of the Dilo in the first

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.480
movie.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.290
The merc's yellow jacket would also have made
the moment a nice call-back to Nedry's scene

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.710
in Jurassic Park.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.149
The Raptor Chaser Twitter account snapped
some photos of a Dilo model at the Pinewood

00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:09.200
workshop for the film.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.560
I suspect the Dilos were cut to make the opening
scene tighter, keep the tension racked up,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.590
and maintain the focus on the T-Rex about
to appear.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.329
It's still a shame we never got to see this
rather colourful and interesting dino again

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:24.999
in the flesh, especially after the hologram
tease at the visitor centre in Jurassic World.

00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:29.180
I don't know if any were taken off the island
as I didn't see any at Lockwood manor, but

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.450
given that Wu has collected samples of a variety
of dinos, it's not impossible that we'll see

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.409
Nedry's killer return in Jurassic World 3.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:41.779
New to the Jurassic franchise is Daniella
Pineda's Zia, the paleo-vet who works with

00:01:41.779 --> 00:01:44.619
Claire and Franklin at the Dinosaur Protection
Group.

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:48.829
And there's an interesting bit of backstory
about Zia that ended up cut from the movie.

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:52.119
Pineda revealed that she filmed a scene before
the main action on the island begins where

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:56.919
she's talking to Owen and says, "Yeah, square
jaw, good bone structure, tall, muscles […] I

00:01:56.919 --> 00:01:59.020
don't date men, but if I did, it would be
you.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.590
It would gross me out, but I'd do it."

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.869
Pineda says the scene wasn't relevant to the
overall story so was chopped as the movie

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:08.660
was running long, but it's also possible it
was cut because it didn't feel very funny

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.660
in the edit.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:14.170
While the line feels like a potentially lazy
way for the screenwriters to point out that

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.719
her character is lesbian, the decision to
delete it is just the latest example of what

00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:22.860
seems to be part of a trend in Hollywood blockbusters
where the reveal of an LGBTQ+ character's

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:28.459
sexuality is cut from the final movie, for
example, Valkyrie's bisexuality in Taika Waititi's

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:32.920
Thor: Ragnarok and Lando's pansexuality in
Solo: A Star Wars Story.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:37.280
The initial cut of Jurassic World 2 was about
two and three quarter hours long so with the

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.640
final runtime clocking in at two hours and
eight minutes, there's more than half an hour

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.209
of footage we never got to see.

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:47.640
Bayona has said that right now there are no
plans to release any deleted or alternate

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.489
scenes on the Blu-ray or DVD, which will doubtless
disappoint many fans.

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:55.590
However, I've done a bit of detective work
and trawled through the official trailers,

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.440
TV spots and behind-the-scenes footage for
clues on what else seems to have been cut

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.230
from Fallen Kingdom.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.450
First up is Ian Malcolm's line
"Here we are talking about dinosaurs again."

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.500
And they also seem to have deleted Malcolm's
classic line which he said in a teaser trailer

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.069
during the Senate Committee hearing.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:13.120
"Life finds a way."

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.819
Maybe they cut this as they felt it was too
on the nose, but personally I would have loved

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:19.640
to have heard him say this again in the film.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.260
Owen also had a couple of lines in the trailers
that were dropped from the final movie.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.860
"This is gonna be awesome."

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.860
"Owen."

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.860
"Ventriloquist?"

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:27.860
"Stop it."

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.860
"You do love a dummy."

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.519
The dummy line should have been included because
it would have made Owen's ventriloquist question

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:33.879
to Claire in the movie funnier and less random.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:38.499
There's a deleted jump scare in the island
control room when Franklin tries to fix a

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:40.209
lightbulb.

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:43.630
"Fixed it."

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.689
"Stop fixing things."

00:03:46.689 --> 00:03:50.329
And I don't recall seeing this footage of
Maisie playing with dinosaur toys in Lockwood

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.830
Manor in the movie.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.379
This would have been additional foreshadowing
of the reveal that Benjamin Lockwood had used

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:59.560
the dinosaur genetic cloning technology he
developed with John Hammond to create Maisie

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.659
as a clone of his dead daughter.

00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:06.159
This camera angle and shot of the Carnotaurus
running at the gyrosphere wasn't in the movie

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:10.530
but there was an alternate take used of the
Carno readying itself to attack before Rexy

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.689
steps in and saves the day.

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:15.909
These trucks driving past a dino skeleton
didn't make it either.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:20.530
And I don't think we saw this underwater shot
of the Mosasaur opening its eye.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:24.360
Let me know if you spotted any other clips
that weren't in the movie.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.389
The Jurassic films have always been pretty
intense monster movies; however, they've always

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:31.300
been accessible to a fairly wide audience
age-wise.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.610
For Fallen Kingdom though, it appears that
some countries have actually censored a number

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.669
of the more violent scenes in the movie.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:42.360
For example, the Indoraptor scene where the
dino rips off Ted Levine's arm was reportedly

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.580
censored in Italy and Korea.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.199
Other scenes that have apparently been banned
are the scene of T-Rex eating the goat when

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:51.020
she's moved into the basement at Lockwood
Manor.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.349
Also censored for some is the moment where
the villainous Eli Mills gets ripped in half

00:04:55.349 --> 00:04:57.810
by T-Rex and Carnotaurus.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:02.610
Even T-Rex's final roar in front of the lion
has reportedly been cut in some countries.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.020
Now, do you think the Dilophosaurus should
have been in the film?

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.180
And are there any other deleted scenes you
wish had been included?

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.200
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

